  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/984ba6ca16cd8ddf25c1bcc68ec04ec353f691f0b9faac78a7fbccc59bf3d9e5.png)\n\nWhat number is missing from the division problem above?",
  "worked_solution": "We have $\\frac{2}{4}$ on the left and $\\frac{2}{20}$ on the right.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133144/assets/b129b90d78fb67dc217534e10db45b5bccc4bea5094bb9242d14e89528b2c891.png)\n\nThe division operation splits each vertical line into $5$ equal parts. So the shaded parts on the left are $5$ times larger than the shaded parts on the right.  \n\nTherefore, the division problem shown is\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{4}÷5=\\frac{2}{20}.\n$$\n\nSo, the missing number is $5.$",
